{number: 75}
{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Nearer, my [F] God, to [C] Thee,
[F] Nearer to [G7] Thee!
[C] E'en though it [F] be a [C] cross
That [G7] raiseth [C] me;
Still all my [F] song shall be,
[C] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [F] God, to [C] Thee,
[F] Nearer [G7] to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Though like the [F] wander-[C] er,
The [F] sun gone [G7] down,
[C] Darkness be [F] over [C] me,
My [G7] rest a [C] stone;
Yet in my [F] dreams I'd be
[C] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [F] God, to [C] Thee,
[F] Nearer [G7] to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] There let the [F] way ap-[C] pear
Steps [F] unto [G7] heav'n;
[C] All that Thou [F] sendest [C] me
In [G7] mercy [C] giv'n:
Angels to [F] beckon me
[C] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [F] God, to [C] Thee,
[F] Nearer [G7] to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Then, with my [F] waking [C] thoughts
Bright [F] with Thy [G7] praise,
[C] Out of my [F] stony [C] griefs,
Bethel [G7] I'll [C] raise;
So by my [F] woes to be
[C] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [F] God, to [C] Thee,
[F] Nearer [G7] to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
